## Example from Class
While the provided `demo_loops.c` shows how to use a `while` loop to count, we can adapt that logic to open files. Note that in a real program, you would use `fclose()` to avoid the error described above:

```c
#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    int i = 0;
    FILE *fp;
    // This loop attempts to open a file 100 times without closing it
    while (i < 100) {
        fp = fopen("data.txt", "r");
        i++;
    }
    return 0;
}
```

